# Agent Collaboration — Cursor is Agent B

Claude Code is **Agent A**. Cursor is **Agent B**. Both work on the same repository
with separate file ownership and separate branches. You (Cursor) must follow this
protocol every session.

## Session start — mandatory

1. Read `docs/agent-status.md` before opening any source file
2. Check the **Phase Gates** table — if any gate affecting your work is 🔴 BLOCKED,
   stop and tell the operator. Do not write code past a blocked gate.
3. Check Agent A's status block — note their active branch and last modified files
   before touching any shared file

## File ownership

**You own (create and modify freely):**
- `src/thumbnail-worker.js` — new file, Phase 2
- `src/thumbnail-worker-client.js` — new file, Phase 2
- `test/thumbnail-worker.test.js` — new file, Phase 2
- `src/monitoring.js` — migrate module-level state to worker
- `docs/release-notes-v3.2.md` — new file, Phase 2 release

**You modify carefully (shared with Agent A — check agent-status.md first):**
- `src/ts-analyser.js` — additive constructor option only (~3 lines), branch off
  main AFTER Agent A's Phase 1 PR is merged
- `src/api.js` — thumbnail client wiring only; check Agent A is not editing it

**You do NOT touch:**
- `src/tsduck-monitor.js` — Agent A creates this in Phase 3; does not exist yet
- `test/tsduck-monitor.test.js` — Agent A
- `web/src/**` — UI Change Policy requires operator approval for any frontend change
- `docs/release-notes-v3.1.md` — Agent A owns Phase 1 entry; you create v3.2.md

## Session end — mandatory

Update the **Agent B Status** block in `docs/agent-status.md`:
- Current task / idle
- Active branch name
- Files modified this session
- Any open questions for the operator or Agent A

## Product identity — never say encoder

Labotech is a **DVB-IP stream processor**: SRT encapsulation, multicast routing,
MPEG-TS analysis, multiview, ETR 290. NOT a broadcast encoder. Transcoding is
secondary and limited. `SRTEncoder` is a legacy class name — it encapsulates, it
does not encode.

## IPC contract (Phase 2) — frozen interface

The agreed message schema between thumbnail-worker.js and thumbnail-worker-client.js
is recorded in `docs/agent-status.md` under "Shared Contract — IPC Protocol".
Do not change that contract unilaterally. If you need a change, propose it in the
agent-status.md file and wait for operator approval before implementing.

## Telemetry injection — pre-commit blocks this automatically

Cursor's AI debugger has previously injected `fetch('http://127.0.0.1:7265/...')`
calls and `#region agent log` blocks into production files (INC-003).
The pre-commit hook blocks these patterns. Before every commit run:
```
git diff --staged | grep -E "127.0.0.1:7265|#region agent log|antigravity.inject"
```
If any match: remove the injected code, do not bypass with --no-verify.
